the doom slayer is essentially a super  soldier a space marine with superhuman  abilities  who can run super fast react with super  speed fall from great heights without  taking damage  and carry large amounts of ammo only  also rips the demon's heads off  and shoves them down their throats and  as though that wasn't already enough  he then chose to stay in hell to battle  demons indefinitely  so yeah he's kind of a badass what can  we take from this though and apply to a  useful  functional workout actually a surprising  amount  but just a quick disclaimer as with many  of these fictional character inspired  workouts  i'm using this as a fun way to discuss  some cool training concepts and ideas  i'm presenting them here for your  further research and consideration  rather than as recommendations these are  out there approaches that may have some  benefit for the wider population  but i'm certainly not claiming these are  ideas for everyone  nor does this represent a complete  training program or prescription  think of it as a thought experiment and  take from it what you will  so the doom slayer is a marine so the  foundation of this training should be  inspired by military training  and this actually translates perfectly  to the traits that we just listed  seeing as the military favor strength  endurance mental toughness  and the ability to carry heavy loads  sound familiar  one of the best methods that the  military used to train these features  specifically  is wrecking rocking involves taking  heavy load strapping it to your back and  then walking long distances  often this is more like a light jog  though on uneven terrain  the simple fact is that infantry need to  be able to perform while carrying heavy  guns and lots of equipment  this is doubly true for doomguy who  seems to carry around an entire arsenal  on his back  rocking of course is one of the best  ways to develop and to test this ability  rocking will build that mental endurance  as well as cardiovascular fitness  strength endurance and even hip and  ankle stability as you adapt to the  uneven ground  it burns a ton of calories in one study  walking with added weight burns 12  more calories than just walking alone  and it's relatively safe  as long as you build up to it gradually  a good recommendation is to start with  roughly 10  of your body weight if you're more  experienced with training  then of course you can go significantly  above this weight rapidly  but start light to get a feel for it  this is also a great option for  incidental training  if you have to walk somewhere throw on a  heavy backpack or a weighted vest and  get some extra bang for your buck  30 minutes is a good amount of time to  start with but you can aim to increase  the distance you cover in this time  and whilst we're carrying heavy stuff  i'd also argue that our doomslayer  workout could benefit from adding  farmers walks  and other forms of loaded carries this  basically means picking up something  heavy holding onto it and walking a  distance  this excellent form of training builds  grip strength which is useful for  ripping demon's jaws off  and if we use one-sided carriers like  the suitcase carry then we'll also be  able to build anti-lateral flexion in  the core  and strengthen the obliques vary walking  with a heavy bag  rocking and carrying something and that  way you'll build even more robust and  rugged performance take it onto uneven  terrain for even more devastating  strength and conditioning  in fact this is starting to look a lot  like something that a user recently  shared with the patrons only bioneers  group on facebook recently  the sprint drag carry or sdc  this is a test of strength endurance and  anaerobic capacity  and it's one of six events used in the  army combat fitness test  here soldiers will sprint to a 25 meter  mark and then back  grab a 90 pound sled and then drag it  backwards to and from the 25 meter line  making sure that the entire sled crosses  the line each time  and then perform a lateral dash sideways  to and from the line  [Music]  finally they run to and from the line  again while holding two 40-pound  [Music]  kettlebells  they then finish on a final sprint  you can try this yourself by finding a  field and using a heavy bag attached to  a rope  mark the distance with cones  and for those interested the other five  events in the army combat fitness test  consist  of three repetition maximum deadlift  standing power throw which is launching  a medicine ball overhead and behind you  hand release push-ups which are push-ups  where you raise your hands from the  ground at the bottom of each movement  thus  losing any momentum the leg tuck is  effectively a tuck front lever but for  reps  whilst using a commando neutral pull-up  grip  and a two mile run and then of course  the sprint drag carry itself  this is actually a pretty interesting  combination of functional movements  and they'd be right at home in a  doomslayer workout  the sdc has a bunch of unique benefits  in itself though for one it's a form of  what's known as cardio acceleration  there's my love of training methods with  awesome names again cardiac acceleration  basically means performing some form of  cardiovascular training  aerobic or anaerobic between sets of  resistance training  rather than resting so this keeps the  heart rate high during your resistance  training and it therefore burns a ton of  calories  and really tests your endurance and it's  also just grueling  of course it's not ideal for primarily  strength or hypertrophy oriented  training  as it does limit the amount you can lift  for our purposes here  energizer money style ripping and  tearing it's perfect  i would also warn against using cardio  acceleration alongside technical or very  heavy lifts  we don't want to be performing deadlifts  whilst exhausted for obvious reasons  as an added bonus the backwoods strag is  also great for the knees  as any fans of ben patrick nizovito's  guy will know  i would argue that you could also place  a crawling dragon here for extra credit  a crawling drag works the upper and  lower body in a way that translates to  faster sprinting  and a stronger core it's also great for  coordinated movement of the limbs  and it's a concentric only exercise  meaning that there's minimal muscle  damage allowing you to train harder  whilst keeping recovery time short  another form of training that's used  regularly in the military  is high rep calisthenics that means high  reps of push-ups pull-ups and the  classic  burpees which i just made a video on  recently they can be trained for high  repetitions with minimal risk of  injury as long as you're in good shape  to begin with they are once again  perfect for improving strength endurance  and work capacity  a doom slayer workout shouldn't be about  lifting something really heavy once  but rather being able to exert lots of  strength for a long amount of time  without tiring out or losing power this  is simply more useful and practical in a  real world setting  burpees are a hybrid exercise that use  both the upper and lower body  this increases the heart rate  significantly as blood needs to get to  the muscles on the opposite sides of the  body  while also building a lot of stability  as you move between positions  and because burpees are explosive they  encourage fast powerful movement  and we can make this even tougher by  adding a little extra weight  in one cool study it was found that  oxygen consumption was increased by an  impressive 100 percent  during military-style training programs  using a weighted vest  alternatively you can make a burpee more  challenging by holding dumbbells and  adding a shoulder press  at the end and this is what we call a  devil press again i discussed this in my  video on burpees  the main devil press certainly seems  appropriate for a doomslayer workout  and in fact hybrid exercises make a lot  of sense in general because they teach  dynamic movement especially when  fatigued  if we're going to be grappling with  demons though then we also need  rotational strength the good news is  that there are countless different  variations on the burpee or devil press  that we can incorporate for similar  benefits  again i listed loads of these in the  recent video  the man maker for example is like a  devil press but with a renegade row  added in  then there are the one legged burpees  there are kicking burpees  dead stop burpees mountain climber  burpees side burpees single arm burpees  spider burpees skate up jump burpees  lateral jumping burpees broad jump  burpees punching burpees  the list goes on and if you want to take  this to the next level then you can set  yourself the challenge of performing any  mixture of these  alongside regular push-ups this becomes  something like a flow but instead of a  movement flow it's more like an  explosive calisthenics  or athletic flow we see flows used a lot  in kettlebell training as well  and this is also where we see a lot of  hybrid exercises  for example you might flow from a  kettlebell swing to a clean to a press  to a kneeling get-up the kettlebell  similarly lends itself perfectly to  training strength endurance and  explosiveness  but even better is that training with  flows like this or any sequence of  movement  creates more need for decision making  and focus the awesome thing about  playing the new doom games in particular  is that they force you to think like the  doom slayer these are intense battles  that don't let up  they require expert resource management  target prioritization  visual processing focus and tactics i  highly suspect that doom eternal in  particular may actually be a very useful  form of brain training  we know from research that any first  person shooter has a lot of benefits for  the brain  but i genuinely believe that do maternal  steps it up a notch  and this is where more complex sequences  of movements have an edge over simple  repetitions  because they force you to focus and they  force you to think about your next  movement  give yourself a string of movements to  perform such as a kick through left kick  through right  burpee 100 up 45 degree bound in each  direction  burpee repeat while this isn't  particularly complex  you're now having to focus carefully on  the movements and keep track of what  you've already done  if you're going to complete the sequence  correctly you just can't let your mind  wander  i've also discussed in the past how  training movements in a more random  order  can actually improve skill acquisition  and retention if you're training for  basketball say  it makes sense to practice a dribble a  pass and a shot  rather than chunking those actions  together as separate drills  and this makes sense it forces you to  concentrate and it's exactly how you  really use those skills in competition  this is another reason that performing  three sets of ten isolation movements  may be a little outmoded the technical  term is contextual interference  and it's worth looking up keep in mind  though that contextual interference  is very much dependent on the nature of  the skill the level of the trainee  and a lot more and with all that said we  could even go a step further  what if we were to throw in brain  training between sets if you have one  minute to recover between sets  why not spend that minute doing a dual  n-back test or some version of the  wisconsin card sorting test  or perhaps a street task not only is  this a time efficient way to train both  body and mind  but it also trains you to think clearly  and calmly during high stress  in this case physiological stress which  can act as a kind of stand-in for  emotional stress  this is one of the differentiators when  it comes to optimal athletic performance  and if there ever is a real crisis  you're able to think clearly  even though you're highly stressed is  what's going to make all the difference  i mean imagine if doom guy was just  whimpering in the corner or just  overwhelmed and distracted  he'd hardly be the cool character that  we think of him as  i've also suggested in the past that  using some form of stop and go test  to begin the next set could be an  effective way to incorporate brain  training  in other words a third party gives you a  signal to begin the next movement  or a dummy and you have to react  accordingly this calls to mind the  military's use of the hooded box test  an exercise that involves placing a  trainee under a hood that completely  blocks their vision and hearing  the hood is then suddenly removed to  reveal an unexpected scenario  this could be a combat scenario or an  old lady asking for the time  the job of the trainee is then to  respond appropriately  and to display situational awareness and  it also desensitizes them to the fear  response over time  one study found that a combination of a  stop signal task a go no-go task  stroop task and visual search task could  be effective at reducing civilian  casualties  among military personnel in short  incorporating brain training in these  ways  could well be an effective method for  building a truly unstoppable machine  like  doomguy  and i'd like to end with a fun idea  training in heat of course doomguy got  most of his training  in hell which is famously hot and this  could actually have an interesting  impact on a person's performance  you see darpa actually has a history of  trying to create super soldiers  check out my old post on the  metabolically dominant soldier program  which is a really awesome name again one  method they experimented with was using  cooling gloves to enhance  performance this works by improving  thermal regulation in the individual  and thus preventing overheating during  training without the use of cooling  gloves  one interesting option that might be  available could be to train with a sauna  suit  in one study it was found that training  in a sauna suit could lead to  improvements in vo2 max  ventilatory threshold and thermal  regulation  often think about sauna suits in  relation to weight loss but it seems  that there might be some significant  performance benefits too  this is all pretty hypothetical and it  likely wouldn't have enough of an effect  to be worth it for most people but it  could explain why the doomslayer is so  unrelenting finally i do also think that  a doomslayer workout should incorporate  some heavy lifting  a power day of big lifts would fit in  here really nicely  after all doom guy is strong and it's  that combination  of amazing strength with grit focus and  endurance that makes him  truly unstoppable so hope you found this  video useful and interesting guys  if you did please leave a like and share  around that really does help me out and  i appreciate it so much  let me know in the comments how you  would program a doomslayer workout  if you like this kind of mind body  training for human performance  then you might like to check out my  ebook and training program super  functional training  the program is designed to improve every  aspect of human performance  from mobility to strength to  explosiveness to focus to decision  making  and more there's a link below and it's  on discount whilst we're all struggling  with a pandemic  i also have an actual print book called  functional training and beyond  that's an introduction to the concept of  functional training and super functional  training  as they pertain to the general  population it has loads of examples of  incredible human performance  whatever the case thank you so much for  watching this one and for all your  support  subscribe if you want to see more like  this and hit the bell notification  button  to make sure you don't miss future  videos thanks guys  and bye for now

